    "turn_text": "Well, there's one family from the Elkhahon area that specifically we were initially started with. And they're not even in Kabul. They're a ways off. And they were a separate challenge for extraction. But we have additional families including a couple that are 80 years old that went to the gate multiple times and no one came out to get them and they were unable to get through. One day it was eight hours of these two 80-year-olds standing in the hot Afghan summer. But they're currently sheltered in, we hope, a safe situation. We also have a pregnant mother, her husband, and her father who repeatedly went to the gate. She was beat, literally kicked in the belly by one of the Taliban, and fortunately, a Afghan special forces on instructions from US special forces all the way back at Fort Bragg. We were in communication with them. Went in and got her and took her back to a friend's apartment, she and her family, and they are currently isolated there waiting for an opportunity to get out, but of course, very traumatized. And those are some of dozens of stories that we've been dealing with. And of course, I've been working with other congressional offices and trying to coordinate opportunities before The HD withdrawal and then obviously I was on the phone with the we in Qatar and other places where they're trying to get the airports opened again and we're trying to figure out how we're going to get flights in. uh... to rescue these people",
