    "turn_text": "well you know that the difference between the devil and the deep blue sea uh... you know there's all kinds of lesser of two evils we could talk about uh... but you don't make peace with your your friends you make peace with your enemies i understand that and and all the way back in the obama administration they began secret negotiations with the telephone but they have not kept their promises and they're not likely to You mentioned that things were worse. In some ways, working with Qatar and working with even the Turks were at least going to know who we're working with and what they're going to say. And in many ways, it's going to be as easy or easier if they say we're going to get this person out and if they're delivered to this point, in some ways that'll be better. But it's a long way off and there's a lot of confusion. And the biggest problem right now is going to be that this administration has already said they're going to give aid to the Afghan people slash government. They've already said that they're going to negotiate with them. Basically, they've already said they're going to pay forms of ransom aid and return for cooperation. And this at a time when there are still freedom fighters holding provinces in the North, the so-called Northern Alliance, that are still a place where schools are open and girls aren't forced in to marriage at 13. So, you know, there's still a civil war going on. And yes, ISIS-K may very well decide that they'd rather have their caliphate rather than the Taliban caliphate. But if you're an Afghan, if you're one of these 37 million people that live there, Neither one of these is going to be good for you. They're both going to be bad, and it's a question of which flavor are bad.",
